<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <POU Name="LifoBuffer" Id="{06690e62-ac15-4ccc-80f2-49e59eb408f7}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[// Provides a simplified LIFO stack interface as an adapter over AnyBuffer
FUNCTION_BLOCK LifoBuffer IMPLEMENTS I_AnyBufferStrategy
VAR
	anyBuffer	  : I_AnyBuffer;
	isInitialized : BOOL := FALSE;
	_overwrite	  : BOOL := FALSE; // When TRUE, Push overwrites oldest element when full
	_reversed	  : BOOL := FALSE; // When TRUE, reverses push/pop direction (PushLeft/PopLeft)
	{attribute 'hide'}
	discardObject : BYTE; // element for discarding elements in overwrite mode
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

LifoBuffer is an adapter (also known as a strategy or facade) that wraps an AnyBuffer instance
to provide a simplified Last-In-First-Out (LIFO) stack interface. Instead of using the full
AnyBuffer API with directional operations (PushLeft/Right, PopLeft/Right), users can simply
Push and Pop elements following standard stack semantics.

### Alternative Names
In computer science, LIFO data structures are commonly called "Stacks". This implementation
could alternatively be named "Stack" or "StackAdapter" for more conventional naming.

### Design Pattern
This implements the **Adapter Pattern** (also Strategy Pattern), which:
- Wraps a more complex interface (I_AnyBuffer) with a simpler, domain-specific interface
- Delegates all operations to the underlying AnyBuffer instance
- Provides semantic clarity: Push/Pop vs PushRight/PopRight
- Allows multiple strategy implementations (FIFO, LIFO, Priority, etc.) over the same buffer

### LIFO Semantics
- **Push(element)**: Adds element using PushRight (reversed=FALSE) or PushLeft (reversed=TRUE)
- **Pop(element)**: Removes element using PopRight (reversed=FALSE) or PopLeft (reversed=TRUE)
- Push and Pop operate on the **same end** of the buffer (unlike FIFO)
- Last element pushed is the first element popped (LIFO behavior)
- Elements maintain insertion order, but retrieval is in reverse order

### Configurable Behavior
The LifoBuffer supports two optional parameters during initialization:

**overwrite parameter:**
- **FALSE (default)**: Push fails when buffer is full, returns FALSE and logs error
- **TRUE**: Push to full buffer automatically removes element to make space (circular buffer behavior)
  - When reversed=FALSE: Removes from front (PopLeft), adds to back (PushRight)
  - When reversed=TRUE: Removes from back (PopRight), adds to front (PushLeft)
  - Removed element is discarded using internal temporary buffer

**reversed parameter:**
- **FALSE (default)**: Standard LIFO - Push to back (PushRight), Pop from back (PopRight)
- **TRUE**: Reversed direction - Push to front (PushLeft), Pop from front (PopLeft)
- Both Push and Pop operate on the **same end** to maintain LIFO semantics

### Operation Mapping
**Standard Mode (overwrite=FALSE, reversed=FALSE):**
```
Push()  -> anyBuffer.PushRight()  // Add to back (right)
Pop()   -> anyBuffer.PopRight()   // Remove from back (right) - LIFO
Clear() -> anyBuffer.Clear()      // Clear all
isEmpty -> anyBuffer.isEmpty      // Check if empty
isFull  -> anyBuffer.isFull       // Check if full
```

**Overwrite Mode (overwrite=TRUE, reversed=FALSE):**
```
Push()  -> if full: anyBuffer.PopLeft(pBufferTemp), then anyBuffer.PushRight()
Pop()   -> anyBuffer.PopRight()   // Remove from back (right)
```

**Reversed Mode (overwrite=FALSE, reversed=TRUE):**
```
Push()  -> anyBuffer.PushLeft()   // Add to front (left)
Pop()   -> anyBuffer.PopLeft()    // Remove from front (left) - LIFO
```

**Overwrite + Reversed Mode (overwrite=TRUE, reversed=TRUE):**
```
Push()  -> if full: anyBuffer.PopRight(pBufferTemp), then anyBuffer.PushLeft()
Pop()   -> anyBuffer.PopLeft()    // Remove from front (left)
```

### Usage Examples

**Standard LIFO Mode (Stack):**
```iecst
VAR
    rawBuffer : ARRAY[0..2] OF DINT;
    buffer : AnyBuffer(pBuffer := rawBuffer,
                       bufferBoundLower := 0,
                       bufferBoundUpper := 2,
                       isBufferPersistent := FALSE);
    lifo : LifoBuffer(anyBuffer := buffer, overwrite := FALSE, reversed := FALSE);
    value : DINT;
END_VAR

// Push elements (adds to back)
value := 100; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100]
value := 200; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200] - 200 added to back
value := 300; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200, 300] - 300 added to back

// Pop elements (LIFO order - newest first)
lifo.Pop(value);   // value = 300 (from back), Stack: [100, 200]
lifo.Pop(value);   // value = 200 (from back), Stack: [100]
lifo.Pop(value);   // value = 100 (from back), Stack: []
```

**Overwrite Mode (Circular Stack):**
```iecst
VAR
    lifo : LifoBuffer(anyBuffer := buffer, overwrite := TRUE, reversed := FALSE);
END_VAR

// Fill buffer
value := 100; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100]
value := 200; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200]
value := 300; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200, 300]

// Push to full buffer overwrites oldest (from opposite end)
value := 400; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [200, 300, 400] - 100 was removed from front
value := 500; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [300, 400, 500] - 200 was removed from front
```

**Reversed Mode (reversed=TRUE):**
```iecst
VAR
    lifo : LifoBuffer(anyBuffer := buffer, overwrite := FALSE, reversed := TRUE);
END_VAR

// Push elements (adds to front using PushLeft)
value := 100; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100]
value := 200; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [200, 100] - 200 added to front
value := 300; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [300, 200, 100] - 300 added to front

// Pop elements (removes from front using PopLeft - LIFO)
lifo.Pop(value);   // value = 300 (from front), Stack: [200, 100]
lifo.Pop(value);   // value = 200 (from front), Stack: [100]
lifo.Pop(value);   // value = 100 (from front), Stack: []
```

### Advantages
- **Simplified interface**: Push/Pop instead of PushRight/PopRight
- **Semantic clarity**: Code intention is clearer with stack terminology
- **Flexibility**: Easy to swap different buffer strategies (FIFO, LIFO, etc.)
- **Type safety**: Enforces LIFO semantics at compile time through interface

### Limitations
- No random access: Cannot peek at arbitrary indices (use AnyBuffer directly if needed)
- No priority queue: Elements are strictly LIFO ordered
- Overwrite mode loses oldest data when buffer is full (from opposite end)
- Combining overwrite and reversed modes creates a circular stack operating from opposite end

### Dependencies
- Requires I_AnyBuffer implementation (e.g., AnyBuffer)
- Uses Trace for error logging and verbose diagnostics
- Implements I_AnyBufferStrategy interface

### Related Patterns
- **FifoBuffer**: Implements queue (First-In-First-Out) semantics
- **PriorityBuffer**: Would implement priority queue with ordered insertion
- **CircularBuffer**: Would implement ring buffer with overwrite semantics
*)
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="Clear" Id="{fd783944-7ee7-4ed4-a036-666a43dcb1bc}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Removes all elements from the stack and resets to empty state
METHOD Clear : BOOL

(*
## Detailed Description

Clears all elements from the underlying buffer, resetting it to an empty state.
After calling Clear, isEmpty will return TRUE and elementCount will be 0.

This operation delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.Clear() method.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Stack was successfully cleared
- **FALSE**: Clear operation failed (e.g., anyBuffer is not initialized)

### Side Effects
- All elements are removed from the buffer
- Element count is reset to 0
- Buffer capacity is restored to maximum
- Logs verbose trace message on success
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[Clear := FALSE;
IF anyBuffer <> 0 THEN
	Clear := anyBuffer.Clear();
	;
END_IF

Trace.Verbose(__POUNAME(), 'executed');]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="FB_Init" Id="{d1d8731d-4d83-4c9f-907f-7fda63eae26f}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Initializes the LIFO stack by injecting the underlying buffer dependency
METHOD FB_Init : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	bInitRetains : BOOL;		// TRUE: the retain variables are initialized (reset warm / reset cold)
	bInCopyCode	 : BOOL;		// TRUE: the instance will be copied to the copy code afterward (online change)
	anyBuffer	 : I_AnyBuffer; // The underlying buffer implementation to wrap
	overwrite	 : BOOL;		// When TRUE, Push overwrites oldest element when full
	reversed	 : BOOL;		// When TRUE, reverses push/pop direction (PushLeft/PopLeft)
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

Initializes the LifoBuffer by injecting the underlying AnyBuffer dependency. This follows
the dependency injection pattern where the buffer implementation is provided during
construction rather than being created internally.

### Initialization Sequence
1. Validates that a valid anyBuffer reference is provided (non-zero pointer)
2. Stores the buffer reference for use by Push, Pop, and other operations
3. Allocates temporary buffer for discarding elements in overwrite mode
4. Sets isInitialized flag to TRUE to enable operations

### Parameters
- **anyBuffer**: Reference to an I_AnyBuffer implementation (e.g., AnyBuffer instance)
  - Must be a valid, initialized buffer
  - This LifoBuffer will delegate all operations to this buffer
- **overwrite**: Controls behavior when pushing to a full buffer
  - **FALSE (default)**: Push returns FALSE and logs error when buffer is full
  - **TRUE**: Push automatically removes an element from opposite end to make space
    - When reversed=FALSE: Removes from front (PopLeft), adds to back (PushRight)
    - When reversed=TRUE: Removes from back (PopRight), adds to front (PushLeft)
  - Discarded element is popped to internal temporary buffer (pBufferTemp)
- **reversed**: Controls the direction of both Push and Pop operations
  - **FALSE (default)**: Push to back (PushRight), Pop from back (PopRight) - standard stack
  - **TRUE**: Push to front (PushLeft), Pop from front (PopLeft) - reversed stack
  - Both operations work on the **same end** to maintain LIFO semantics

### Return Value
Returns BOOL but value is not evaluated by the runtime. Always call with valid anyBuffer.

### Usage Example
```iecst
VAR
    rawBuffer : ARRAY[0..9] OF DINT;
    buffer : AnyBuffer(pBuffer := rawBuffer,
                       bufferBoundLower := 0,
                       bufferBoundUpper := 9,
                       isBufferPersistent := FALSE);
    lifo : LifoBuffer(anyBuffer := buffer,
                      overwrite := FALSE,
                      reversed := FALSE);
END_VAR
```

### Important Notes
- Must provide a valid anyBuffer reference, otherwise Push/Pop will fail
- The underlying buffer must already be initialized before passing to FB_Init
- A temporary buffer (pBufferTemp) is allocated internally for discarding elements in overwrite mode
- pBufferTemp is automatically deallocated in FB_exit
- Overwrite mode is useful when newest data is more important than oldest
- Reversed mode changes the operational direction of both Push and Pop
- Combining overwrite=TRUE and reversed=TRUE creates a circular stack operating from the opposite end
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF anyBuffer <> 0 THEN
	THIS^.anyBuffer := anyBuffer;
	_overwrite		:= overwrite;
	_reversed		:= reversed;
	isInitialized	:= TRUE;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="isEmpty" Id="{4069a5ef-c7ff-4f4f-9171-3e476a32891c}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Returns TRUE if the stack contains no elements
PROPERTY isEmpty : BOOL

(*
## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the stack is empty (contains no elements), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isEmpty property.

Use this property to check if Pop operation would succeed before attempting to
remove an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Stack is empty (elementCount = 0)
- **FALSE**: Stack contains one or more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT lifo.isEmpty THEN
    lifo.Pop(value);  // Safe to pop
END_IF
```
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{f9a815dc-dc24-495d-b9f2-02ef7661d838}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[isEmpty := anyBuffer.isEmpty;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="isFull" Id="{ae2ca38a-cd60-4366-8eb3-6ddbaa8b5d66}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Returns TRUE if the stack is at maximum capacity
PROPERTY isFull : BOOL

(*
## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the stack is full (at maximum capacity), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isFull property.

Use this property to check if Push operation would succeed before attempting to
add an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Stack is full (elementCount = capacity)
- **FALSE**: Stack has space for more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT lifo.isFull THEN
    value := 100;
    lifo.Push(value);  // Safe to push
END_IF
```
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{1dd9dd55-b31c-4b32-acae-0c514071e75c}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[isFull := anyBuffer.isFull;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Method Name="Pop" Id="{43d95542-b9b4-4dd3-91aa-39b14c6b0593}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Removes and retrieves an element from the stack (LIFO pop operation)
{attribute 'hasanytype'}
METHOD Pop : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	element : ANY; // Variable to receive the popped element
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

Removes and retrieves an element from the stack. The behavior depends on the 'reversed'
initialization parameter, but always maintains LIFO (Last-In-First-Out) semantics.

**When reversed = FALSE (default mode):**
- Removes element from the back (right side, highest index)
- Delegates to anyBuffer.PopRight()
- Standard stack behavior - last pushed is first popped

**When reversed = TRUE (reversed mode):**
- Removes element from the front (left side, index 0)
- Delegates to anyBuffer.PopLeft()
- Reversed direction but still LIFO - last pushed (to front) is first popped

### Operation Sequence
1. Validates that the buffer has been initialized
2. Validates that element size matches the buffer's configured element size
3. Checks that the stack is not empty
4. Removes element using PopRight (default) or PopLeft (reversed) based on reversed setting
5. Copies the element value to the output parameter
6. For PopLeft: Shifts remaining elements left; For PopRight: No shifting needed
7. Logs verbose trace on success or error trace on failure

### Standard Mode Example (reversed = FALSE)
```iecst
// Push to back, Pop from back (LIFO)
value := 100; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100]
value := 200; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200] - 200 added to back
value := 300; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200, 300] - 300 added to back

lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 300 (from back), Stack: [100, 200]
lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 200 (from back), Stack: [100]
lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 100 (from back), Stack: []
```

### Reversed Mode Example (reversed = TRUE)
```iecst
// Push to front, Pop from front (LIFO)
value := 100; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100]
value := 200; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [200, 100] - 200 added to front
value := 300; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [300, 200, 100] - 300 added to front

lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 300 (from front), Stack: [200, 100]
lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 200 (from front), Stack: [100]
lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 100 (from front), Stack: []
```

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Element was successfully popped and copied to element parameter
- **FALSE**: Pop operation failed (see error conditions)

### Error Conditions
- Returns FALSE and logs error if buffer was not initialized
- Returns FALSE and logs error if element size doesn't match buffer element size
- Returns FALSE and logs error if stack is empty (no elements to pop)
- Returns FALSE and logs error if underlying PopLeft or PopRight operation fails

### Parameters
- **element**: Must be a writable variable (not a literal) of the correct size
  - Must match the buffer's configured element size
  - Will receive the popped element value on success

### Side Effects
- Removes one element from the stack
- Decrements element count by 1
- For reversed=FALSE (PopRight): No element shifting required
- For reversed=TRUE (PopLeft): Shifts remaining elements one position to the left
- Logs verbose trace message on success
- Logs error trace message on failure
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[Pop := FALSE;
IF NOT isInitialized THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Buffer was not initialized yet, execute method .init() at least once');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// valid sized element?
IF element.diSize <> anyBuffer.Configuration.elementSize THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Passed element to pop to is of improper size');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// retrieve element from buffer if there is any left
IF NOT isEmpty THEN
	IF _reversed THEN
		// Reversed: pop from front (left) - LIFO
		Pop := anyBuffer.PopLeft(element);
	ELSE
		// Standard: pop from back (right) - LIFO
		Pop := anyBuffer.PopRight(element);
	END_IF
ELSE
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Attempt to pop from empty buffer');
END_IF

// Pop was ok, trace message
IF Pop THEN
	Trace.Verbose(__POUNAME(), 'executed');
ELSE
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'FAILED');
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Push" Id="{016926d4-ed93-44d8-a1a4-cd7737eb0500}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Adds a new element to the stack (LIFO push operation, direction depends on reversed setting)
{attribute 'hasanytype'}
METHOD Push : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	element : ANY; // Element to add to the stack
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

Adds a new element to the stack. The push direction and overwrite behavior depend on
the 'reversed' and 'overwrite' initialization parameters. Push and Pop operate on the
**same end** of the buffer to maintain LIFO semantics.

**Push Direction (reversed parameter):**
- **reversed = FALSE (default)**: Delegates to anyBuffer.PushRight() - adds to back/right
- **reversed = TRUE**: Delegates to anyBuffer.PushLeft() - adds to front/left

**Overwrite Behavior (overwrite parameter):**
- **overwrite = FALSE (default)**: Push fails if buffer is full, returns FALSE and logs error
- **overwrite = TRUE (circular buffer mode)**: Push succeeds even when buffer is full
  - When reversed=FALSE: Removes element from front (PopLeft to pBufferTemp), then adds to back (PushRight)
  - When reversed=TRUE: Removes element from back (PopRight to pBufferTemp), then adds to front (PushLeft)
  - Discarded element is popped to internal temporary buffer and dropped
  - Useful for scenarios where newest data is more important than oldest

### Operation Sequence

**Standard Mode (overwrite = FALSE, reversed = FALSE):**
1. Validates that the buffer has been initialized
2. Validates that element size matches the buffer's configured element size
3. Checks that the stack is not full (has available capacity)
4. If full: Returns FALSE and logs error
5. If not full: Adds element to the back using PushRight
6. Logs verbose trace on success or error trace on failure

**Standard Mode with Reversed (overwrite = FALSE, reversed = TRUE):**
1. Validates that the buffer has been initialized
2. Validates that element size matches the buffer's configured element size
3. Checks that the stack is not full (has available capacity)
4. If full: Returns FALSE and logs error
5. If not full: Adds element to the front using PushLeft
6. Logs verbose trace on success or error trace on failure

**Overwrite Mode (overwrite = TRUE, reversed = FALSE):**
1. Validates that the buffer has been initialized
2. Validates that element size matches the buffer's configured element size
3. If buffer is full: Removes oldest element from front using PopLeft (discards to pBufferTemp)
4. Adds new element to the back using PushRight
5. Logs verbose trace on success or error trace on failure

**Overwrite Mode with Reversed (overwrite = TRUE, reversed = TRUE):**
1. Validates that the buffer has been initialized
2. Validates that element size matches the buffer's configured element size
3. If buffer is full: Removes oldest element from back using PopRight (discards to pBufferTemp)
4. Adds new element to the front using PushLeft
5. Logs verbose trace on success or error trace on failure

### Standard Mode Example (overwrite = FALSE)
```iecst
// Starting with empty stack
value := 100; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100]
value := 200; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200]
value := 300; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200, 300]

// Pop operations retrieve in LIFO order (newest first)
lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 300 (last pushed)
lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 200 (second to last)
lifo.Pop(value);  // Returns 100 (first pushed)
```

### Overwrite Mode Example (overwrite = TRUE)
```iecst
// Assuming buffer capacity is 3
value := 100; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100]
value := 200; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200]
value := 300; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [100, 200, 300] - full

// Push to full buffer overwrites oldest (from opposite end)
value := 400; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [200, 300, 400] - 100 removed from front
value := 500; lifo.Push(value);  // Stack: [300, 400, 500] - 200 removed from front
```

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Element was successfully pushed to the stack
- **FALSE**: Push operation failed (see error conditions)

### Error Conditions
- Returns FALSE and logs error if buffer was not initialized
- Returns FALSE and logs error if element size doesn't match buffer element size
- Returns FALSE and logs error if stack is full AND overwrite is FALSE
- Returns FALSE and logs error if underlying PushRight or PushLeft operation fails
- In overwrite mode, Push should always succeed unless buffer is not initialized or element size is wrong

### Parameters
- **element**: Must be a writable variable (not a literal) of the correct size
  - Must match the buffer's configured element size
  - Value will be copied into the stack

### Side Effects

**Standard Mode (overwrite = FALSE):**
- Adds one element to the stack
- No shifting of existing elements required (for PushRight)
- Shifts elements right (for PushLeft when reversed=TRUE)
- Increments element count by 1
- Decrements available capacity by 1
- Logs verbose trace message on success
- Logs error trace message on failure

**Overwrite Mode (overwrite = TRUE):**
- If buffer is full: Removes oldest element from opposite end first
- Adds new element to the push end
- Element count remains constant when overwriting
- Logs verbose trace message on success
- Logs error trace message on failure

### Performance Considerations
- **Standard mode (reversed=FALSE)**: O(1) - PushRight is constant time, no shifting
- **Standard mode (reversed=TRUE)**: O(n) - PushLeft requires shifting all elements right
- **Overwrite mode (reversed=FALSE)**: O(n) when full (PopLeft with shifting + PushRight)
- **Overwrite mode (reversed=TRUE)**: O(n) when full (PopRight O(1) + PushLeft O(n))
- **Overwrite mode**: O(1) or O(n) when not full (depends on reversed setting)
- Pop operation with reversed=FALSE has O(1) complexity (PopRight, no shifting)
- Pop operation with reversed=TRUE has O(n) complexity (PopLeft with shifting)
- Trade-off: reversed=FALSE optimizes both Push and Pop, reversed=TRUE makes Push slower
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[Push := FALSE;
IF NOT isInitialized THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Buffer was not initialized yet, execute method .init() at least once');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// valid sized element pushed?
IF element.diSize <> anyBuffer.Configuration.elementSize THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Pushed element is of improper size');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// handle full buffer based on overwrite setting
IF isFull THEN
	IF _overwrite THEN
		// Overwrite mode: remove element from opposite end to make space (discard to pBufferTemp)
		IF _reversed THEN
			// Reversed: remove from back before adding to front
			anyBuffer.PopRight(discardObject, TRUE);
		ELSE
			// Standard: remove from front before adding to back
			anyBuffer.PopLeft(discardObject, TRUE);
		END_IF
	ELSE
		// Standard mode: fail and log error
		Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Attempt to push to full buffer');
		RETURN;
	END_IF
END_IF

// add element based on direction setting (same end as Pop for LIFO)
IF _reversed THEN
	// Reversed: add to front (left)
	Push := anyBuffer.PushLeft(element);
ELSE
	// Standard: add to back (right)
	Push := anyBuffer.PushRight(element);
END_IF

// Push was ok, trace message
IF Push THEN
	Trace.Verbose(__POUNAME(), 'executed');
ELSE
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'FAILED');
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>